{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1287847-ainur-preliminary-thoughts","id":1287847,"title":"Ainur preliminary thoughts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-02-13T21:49:59-08:00","id":1287847,"title":"Ainur preliminary thoughts","content":"Pantheon motif: Faith and determination can work miracles.<br /> <br /> Virtues Responsibility and Joy<br /> <br /> The Ainur are motivated both but the joy of Eru\u2019s creation and also by the responsibility of their position as stewards. They fear to do more harm with their meddling than good and approach everything from the most cautious of attitudes. In some cases their particular joy may be frustrated by conflicts with their responsibility and they turn aside from their roles of steward to selfishly engage their desires as Morgoth and Sauron has. In other cases their responsibility may lead them to forsake the things that bring them joy for fear of destroying them. Withdrawing from the world as the Valar have.<br /> <br /> Cosmology - The Ainur are fated to remain with the world until it comes to an end. As a pantheon they have neither an Underworld nor an Overworld but live in numerous terra incognitae of variable greatness ranging from the former Rivendell to great Valinor, which can only be found by those who remember the way from when the world was still flat.<br /> <br /> Scions - almost all Ainur scions are Incarnate Maiar who have set about to trickle back into The World either to experience it for themselves or to attend to the will of Eru.<br /> <br /> Technically speaking those are the only Ainur. But some Elves could be argued to have reached God tier for such accomplishments as building the Silmarils or piloting a ship that holds such a jewel as a star in the sky. Also. Some humans have reached the Demigod tier but as they are not bound by Arda\u2019s Fate all Men move on rather than become lasting cosmic figures of the world. Still it is possible to include some Elves and Men as Chosen, especially those that are educated by one of the Maiar.<br /> <br /> It should be noted that One who had no human blood was granted the Gift of Man, Luthien. So it is conceivable that a human could appeal to Eru in someway and turn aside from the Gift of Man. In doing so this person would no longer be human as the nature of their spirit would have changed. Humans are by definition free of the bonds of Arda so if a human becomes bound to Arda they are no longer bound. This keeps the God tier for the most powerful and cosmically impactful of Ainur and Elves but still allows for an PC that starts human to advance to God tier. Though they at this point would suffer the doom to see the things that bring them joy eventually and be replaced by things that would also later die off.<br /> <br /> Elves also have a reincarnation system and thus can be played as Incarnates.<br /> <br /> There is only record of one born scion in the Legendarium, Luthien, but her existence indicates that the Ainur and Eru don\u2019t consider it a matter of cosmic importance. Also elves and men less touched by the lies of Morgoth may be closer to the original intentions of those people and be considered born scions. As a note, in order to have a child an Ainur has to Incarnate as either a human or elf and their children will be considered of the appropriate people.<br /> <br /> Created scions are a whole issue though. Trying to create life through means outside of the will of Eru is liable to lead an Ainur to fall. Aule managed it with the dwarves as it became apparent that he created them to add to Eru\u2019s creation rather than usurp it. Created scions either have been similarly approved by Eru or else have severe issues resulting from their creator basically playing Frankenstein.<br /> <br /> Titans. Morgoth - Chaos. Fecundity, Submission. Frustrated by the constraints placed upon him by Eru, Melkor slowly became more and more twisted until he fell entirely. He started trying to replace elements of Eru\u2019s creation with his own and we he failed in that he began to try and twist Eru\u2019s creations toward his own designs. As each of these became more and more twisted and ugly, he finally just desired to torment Eru\u2019s creations.<br /> <br /> Sauron - Deception (Forge suggested as better option). Dominance, Submission. Sauron fell through his love for Melkor and the greatness that he used to be. He applied all his craft and power toward achieving Melkor\u2019s goals. Even as Melkor became Morgoth Sauron was unable to see as his liege grew more mad over time. When Morgoth was finally banished he had a moment of regret but pride prevented him from returning to face Manwe\u2019s judgment. From this point on he grew increasingly insane until he was finally defeated. He exists now as a ghost of a ghost. Unlike Morgoth, whose Iron Crown was reforged into manacles, Sauron\u2019s One Ring was destroyed and he had no way of gaining a new fana with which to influence the world. Though perhaps some sorcerer might bind him into a corpse or wolf and open the path for him again by accident.<br /> <br /> Ungoliant - Beasts(spider) (Darkness suggested as a better option. I also considered Passion(Hunger)). Rapacity, Fecundity. Little is known of Ungoliant save that age and her children seek to devour the force of creation. She is not one of Morgoth\u2019s creatures and indeed grew to threaten him at one time. Some suspect that she is not even if the Ainur but something else entirely.<br /> <br /> Feanor - Passion(Vengeance). Rapacity, Dominance. Feanor is not Ainur but is an elf, though his impact on Arda places him here. An elf of great power and wrath who at one time battled Morgoth himself for a long time before being slain. Feanor and his sons are bound by oaths to retrieve the Silmarils and slay all who would stand between them and that goal. They are first kinslayers and while some tried to redeem themselves they often became as great evils as Morgoth\u2019s lieutenants were. As elves it is possible that they could reincarnate anew and once again begin their campaign of destructive vengeance. For now, though their spirits remain in the Halls of Mandos.<br /> <br /> Pantheon Purview - Craft (filler name). Magic in Arda is a term used by the less educated to refer to the crafts of the learned and also the deceptions of the Enemy. The results of these skills seem supernatural to onlookers but in reality all that has been done is to allow nature to work in complete and total efficiency toward the desired of the end of the one performing the spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3961,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","user":"Thrythlind","date":". 02-14-2019, 05:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","name":"Thrythlind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T22:42:52-08:00","id":1287860,"title":"","content":"Personally I\u2019d make Sauron a Forge Titan. Besides the rings, I\u2019d play up the industrialization ravaging Middle Earth angle that Tolkien was getting at. Deception can also make sense, though we only get that aspect of him in the Silmarillion, not at all in LotR, which implies to me while he has that Purview, it doesn\u2019t drive his actions the way Forge does.<br /> <br /> Ungoliant is definitely a Darkness Titan. Her shape as a giant spider is comparatively incidental to her identity as Incarnate Night.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-13T22:49:35-08:00","id":1287862,"title":"","content":"Good points. Yeah. Sauron as Forge makes more sense. I almost did Ungoliant as Passion (Hunger) But Darkness works too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","name":"Thrythlind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T01:37:08-08:00","id":1287888,"title":"","content":"I admit it took me until I saw &quot;Maiar&quot; to place what this was. Maybe you could change the title to &quot;The Ainur of Middle Earth&quot; for those who aren't totally up to date on our Tolkien Cosmology Terminology?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T02:10:08-08:00","id":1287890,"title":"","content":"Sadly, I can't change the title.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","name":"Thrythlind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T07:19:44-08:00","id":1287929,"title":"","content":"Neall mentioned in an interview that not all Titans are embodiments of a single Purview - some of them have a few, depending on whether or not they're &quot;Emanations.&quot; Ungoliant, for example, could have all three of the possible Purviews mentioned, as all of them fit very well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12689-creepyshutin","name":"CreepyShutIn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T09:03:34-08:00","id":1287964,"title":"","content":"On 1e, there was a real difference between gods and titans, and following that rules Morgoth is not a Titan, but the most powerful god (supposing the gods are limited to the Valar), as he have the same origin.<br /> <br /> I am not a Tolkien expert, actually I know little more than what is told on LotR, but as Insee, Valar are Gods, Maiar Demigods and some of the free people (Elves, Ents and a few Giants, not sure) are natural Heroes. Humans (and others) can ascend to heroic and Demigos stats, as well as Elves (and others) can ascend to demigods (Galadriel), but it\u2019s impossible to became much more powerful than a Maiar,<br /> As I said, I am no expert, so I may be deeply wrong...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T09:16:28-08:00","id":1287969,"title":"","content":"If anyone's looking for good Tolkien lore analysis, I recommend the YouTube channel Men of the West. Civilization Ex also has good stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T10:02:18-08:00","id":1287979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CreepyShutIn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1287847-ainur-preliminary-thoughts?p=1287929#post1287929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neall mentioned in an interview that not all Titans are embodiments of a single Purview - some of them have a few, depending on whether or not they're &amp;quot;Emanations.&amp;quot; Ungoliant, for example, could have all three of the possible Purviews mentioned, as all of them fit very well.</div> </div> </div> </div>He mentioned they can wield multiple Purviews. They all still have one dominant Purview that drives their nature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T11:33:12-08:00","id":1288011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1287847-ainur-preliminary-thoughts?p=1287979#post1287979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> He mentioned they can wield multiple Purviews. They all still have one dominant Purview that drives their nature.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I see. Then Ungoliant probably has Darkness. Seems the most central.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12689-creepyshutin","name":"CreepyShutIn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T14:17:59-08:00","id":1288074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1287847-ainur-preliminary-thoughts?p=1287964#post1287964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On 1e, there was a real difference between gods and titans, and following that rules Morgoth is not a Titan, but the most powerful god (supposing the gods are limited to the Valar), as he have the same origin.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is a 2E-themed writeup. :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T14:32:21-08:00","id":1288079,"title":"","content":"Regarding levels of power:<br /> <br /> One of Feanor's sons struck Morgoth an injury that permanently disabled him in a very long duel. Feanor himself was considered the greatest of the Noldor and Galadriel was second only to him. However, Galadriel's power was not typically martially directed so she might not have been able to replicate the feats of war. By the time we see her Lord of the Rings she's had at least one child which takes a heavy toll on both elven parents (one of the reasons elves don't have many kids, another being that they tend to get less and less interested in sexual activity as time goes on) but especially the mother, so her power might have been less than it used to be.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","name":"Thrythlind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-14T14:34:10-08:00","id":1288080,"title":"","content":"Yes, this is a 2e writeup so I assigned titan status to individuals who shook up the cosmology and who had hugely fixated personalities. If I were honest, Sauron is the one that least deserves to be there because he didn't cause near as much shake-up as any of the other three. The most I could point to was the sinking of Numenor and the sinking of the world...but that was more Sauron's actions provoking Numenor to do something that provoked Eru to shake-up the cosmology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3961,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","user":"Thrythlind","date":". 02-14-2019, 05:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","name":"Thrythlind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T21:53:29-07:00","id":1297449,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">I don't know if anyone is still interested in this, but I did small write ups for the Ainur, and I thought I'd put them here:</span></span> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ainur - Gods of Middle-Earth</span></span></b></span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Asset Skill: Leadership, Occult</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Virtues: Responsibility vs Joy</span></span></span></div> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Manw\u00eb, Lord of the Breath of Arda</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(S\u00falimo, M\u00e2nawen\u00fbz, Valahiru, Aran Einior)</span></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Callings: Creator, Leader, Guardian</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Purviews: Beasts (Bird), Darkness, Epic Dexterity, Fortune, Order, Sky, Sun</span></span></li> </ul><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ulmo, Lord of Waters</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(Ulub\u00f4z, Ullub\u00f4z)</span></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Callings: Liminal, Creator, Guardian</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Purviews: Artistry (Music), Beasts (Whale), Darkness, Earth, Epic Stamina, Epic Strength, Passion (Fear), Water</span></span></li> </ul><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Aul\u00eb, The Smith</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(Mahal, Oli, N\u00e1vatar)</span></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Callings: Creator, Sage, Lover</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Purviews: Earth, Epic Stamina, Epic Strength, Forge, Moon, Sun</span></span></li> </ul><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Orom\u00eb, The Great Rider</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(Aldaron, Araw, Ar\u00f4m\u00eaz, Tavros, B\u00e9ma, Tauron, Wadfrea, Huntena Frea, Wealdafrea)</span></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Callings: Hunter, Liminal, Warrior</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Purviews: Beasts (Wolf, Horse, Ox), Epic Dexterity, Fertility, Moon, Order, Passion (Wrath), War, Wild</span></span></li> </ul><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mandos, Doomsman of the Valar</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(N\u00e1mo, Bannoth, Badhron, The Judge, The Just, Nefrea, Neoaerna Hlaford, Morimando, Vefantur)</span></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Callings: Judge, Liminal, Guardian</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Purviews: Chaos, Death, Earth, Fortune, Order</span></span></li> </ul><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Irmo, Master of Dreams and Illusions</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(L\u00f3rien, L\u00farin)</span></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Callings: Lover, Liminal, Sage</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Purviews: Darkness, Death, Deception, Fertility, Fortune, Passion (Hope, Love)</span></span></li> </ul><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Tulkas, Champion of the Valar</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(Tulukast\u0101z, Astaldo, Tulcus, The Valiant)</span></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Callings: Warrior, Guardian, Judge</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Purviews: Epic Dexterity, Epic Stamina, Epic Strength, Passion (Valor), War</span></span></li> </ul><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Varda, Queen of the Stars</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">(Elbereth, Tintall\u00eb, Gilthoniel, Star-Kindler, Lady of the Stars, Elent\u00e1ri, Fanuilos, Snow-White, The Kindler, Elbereth Gilthoniel)</span></span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Callings: Creator, Leader, Sage</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Purviews: Beauty, Fortune, Moon, Stars, Sun, Water</span></span></li> </ul><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Yavanna, Giver of Fruits</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><s